Z||000000||bHooper||05-06-2000||09:06 PM||||i have finally reasembled the tranny and the engine and was wondering how much "play" should there be in the release arm?  It moves back and forth freely but as I push it towards the pressure plate I do not get a "springy" feel.  Is this normal?  If there is a fair amount of movement, how does the slave  cylinder make this thing work?<P>Since I have no prior experience with these things, I just wanted some other opinions.<P>Thanks,<BR>hoop||||reg||5
Z||000001||Phil||05-06-2000||10:57 PM||||That's the way it should behave. You wouldn't be able to push in the clutch by hand, Arnold  the Terminator wouldn't be able do it either. When you hook up the slave the push rod should be just about perpendicular to the clutch arm.||||reg||1
Z||000002||bHooper||05-07-2000||07:56 AM||||Well thats good, sounds like nothing shifted (the t/o bearing didnt move outa place) when I put the tranny on the other night.<P>that was, of course a slight fear... which now pales in comparison to the problem of not haveing a fiero shift release arm!<P>hoop<p>[This message has been edited by bHooper (edited 05-07-2000).]||||reg||1
